393	    return `
394	Topic-specific requirements for linear function visuals:
395	- Make the real-time formula y = ax + b visually prominent, with a and b values updated live.
396	- Draw a coordinate system with readable x/y axes, tick labels, and a single clear line.
397	- Label the y-intercept point at x = 0 and connect it to b.
398	- Show a slope triangle on or near the line with Delta x = 1 and Delta y = a.
399	- When a changes, make the rotation/tilt change visually obvious and update a short observation sentence.
400	- When b changes, make the parallel vertical shift visually obvious and update a short observation sentence.
